-# STARFRONT: Pocket Command 3D — Vertical Slice 001
+# STARFRONT: Pocket Command 3D — Vertical Slice 001 (R2.1)
 
-A playable, mobile-first 3D Tactical Real-Time Strategy (RTS) vertical slice built with **TypeScript** and **Three.js (WebGL2)** that reuses the authoritative simulation rules from the original 2D prototype while cleanly separating simulation from 3D visualization.
+Playable mobile-first 3D tactical RTS vertical slice. Authoritative deterministic Game Core + Three.js WebGL2 renderer.
 
----
+**Release Gate R2.1:** see [`RELEASE_GATE_R2_1.md`](./RELEASE_GATE_R2_1.md). Official Three.js production + automated browser verification are **PASS**. Physical iPhone Safari QA remains **NOT RUN**.
 
-## 1. Architecture Overview
+## Architecture
 
-The project enforces five strict architectural boundaries:
-
-1. **Game Core (`src/core/specs.ts`, `src/core/simulation.ts`)**
-   - Owns the authoritative, deterministic 60 Hz fixed-timestep simulation (`FIXED_DT = 1 / 60`).
-   - Manages 3 independent factions (`player`, `enemy`, `bot2`), unit/building stats, GDP economy, supply & power caps, target acquisition via a 2D spatial hash grid, directional/high-ground combat damage, bridge pathing, outpost capture, and victory/defeat conditions.
-   - Zero dependency on Three.js objects or rendering frame rate.
-2. **World Adapter (`src/adapter/worldAdapter.ts`)**
-   - Maps 2D simulation coordinates `(game.x, game.y)` to 3D world space `(x, terrainHeight, z)`.
-   - Performs smooth position, hull-yaw, and turret-yaw interpolation (`alpha`) between fixed simulation ticks without mutating authoritative state.
-3. **Three.js 3D Scene & Low-Poly Model Factory (`src/render/models3d.ts`, `src/render/scene3d.ts`)**
-   - Builds the `1200 × 800` 3D battlefield with raised high-ground plateaus, river channel, functional central armored bridge, tactical road network, rock obstacles, and 3 faction bases.
-   - Generates procedural low-poly 3D meshes with shared geometries and materials for `Infantry` (`marine`, `trooper`), `APC`, `Tank`, `HQ`, `Barracks`, `Factory`, and `Turret`.
-   - Provides `Eco`, `Balanced`, and `Quality` mobile performance presets.
-4. **Input Controller (`src/input/inputController.ts`)**
-   - Uses Pointer Events and `THREE.Raycaster` ground-plane intersection.
-   - Supports tap-to-select, tap-ground-to-move, tap-enemy-to-attack, drag-box multi-selection, 1-finger pan mode, 2-finger pinch zoom anchored at the touch midpoint, 2-finger pan, camera rotation, and multi-touch cancellation safety (secondary touches never trigger accidental move or attack orders).
-5. **Tactical HUD (`index.html`, `src/main.ts`)**
-   - Compact iPhone-first overlay displaying GDP, income rate, Supply, Power, Outpost ownership, selected unit count/HP, unit production buttons, Move/Attack-Move/Hold/Retreat commands, camera controls, live FPS counter, and quality preset toggle.
+1. **Game Core** (`src/core/specs.ts`, `src/core/simulation.ts`) — deterministic 60 Hz sim; no Three.js dependency  
+2. **World Adapter** (`src/adapter/worldAdapter.ts`) — 2D→3D mapping + interpolation  
+3. **Renderer** (`src/render/*`) — official `three@0.160.0` WebGL2 + hardware instancing  
+4. **Input** (`src/input/inputController.ts`) — pointer, pinch, two-finger rotate  
+5. **HUD / boot** (`index.html`, `src/boot.ts`, `src/main.ts`) — iPhone-safe HUD + WebGL warm-up before official renderer boot  
 
----
+Protected Game Core files are byte-locked (see release gate matrix).
 
-## 2. Build & Usage Instructions
+## Official production (required for R2.1)
 
-### Option A — Standard Vite / Vitest Workflow (Environment with npm registry access)
+```bash
+npm ci
+npx --no-install tsc --noEmit
+npm run build:vite
+node scripts/verify-official-three.mjs   # must print verdict PASS
+npm test                                # deterministic + shim + offline suites
+npm run test:browser                    # headless Chrome vs Vite dist/
+```
+
+Dev server (uncommon port):
 
 ```bash
-cd starfront-3d-vertical-slice
-npm install
-npm run test      # Runs deterministic simulation & adapter suite via Vitest
-npm run dev       # Starts local Vite dev server
-npm run build     # Compiles TypeScript and builds static bundle into dist/
+npm run dev    # http://127.0.0.1:3847
 ```
 
-### Option B — Offline Zero-Dependency Build & Verification (Sandbox / Air-Gapped Environment)
+## Offline / air-gapped standalone (NOT official Three.js proof)
 
-When outbound internet access or npm package installation is disabled:
+```bash
+npm run build:standalone
+# Writes dist/standalone-shim.html + dist/offline-shim/three/
+# Does NOT modify node_modules/three
+```
+
+## iPhone Safari LAN preview
+
+After `npm run build:vite`:
 
 ```bash
-cd starfront-3d-vertical-slice
-node scripts/build-standalone.mjs   # Transpiles TS modules & builds dist/index.html + dist/core-bundle.mjs
-node tests/run-tests.mjs            # Runs 10 deterministic regression tests + 50/100/200-unit stress benchmarks
+npm run preview:iphone
 ```
 
-To play the production build directly in any desktop or mobile browser, open `dist/index.html` (or the standalone artifact `starfront_3d_vertical_slice.html`).
+Serves `dist/` over ephemeral HTTPS for a device on the same LAN. Thermal / sustained-FPS validation is **NOT RUN** until performed on physical hardware.
+
+## Scripts
+
+| Script | Purpose |
+|--------|---------|
+| `build:vite` | Official production build (npm `three@0.160.0`) |
+| `verify:official-three` | Import-graph / package proof |
+| `test` / `test:core` / `test:shim` / `test:offline` | Separated Node test suites |
+| `test:browser` | Real Chromium WebGL2 verification |
+| `build` / `build:standalone` | Offline shim IIFE only |
